@capability-norm-design-case @oracle-python @comparison-exact
Feature: Every EN 1995 catalogue entry is usable from a document as a design case
  A design case (`cases[]` of the snapshot) names a catalogue entry T-nn and stores typed inputs. The typed vocabulary (`🧬️schema/⚖️kernel/📇️catalogue/📚️inputs/🔣️.json`) gives every input its stored unit, English and German label, bounds and choices. Executed by `🧬️schema/🧪️tests/⚖️compliance/🦀️.rs` (module `design_case_bridge`) and the independent oracle `🔮️oracles/🗂️design-case/🐍️.py`; the shared law is specified in `⚖️compliance/🧰️design-case/🧪️tests/🥒️scenarios/🥒️.feature`.

  Further specification assertions, asserted by the Rust unit tests of the crate and not by the platform adapters:
  - Every declared input has a typed vocabulary row: Given the 68 catalogue entries of the kernel sources When the inputs of each entry are looked up in the vocabulary for that entry Then every input resolves, rows are unique per key and scope, and every scope names an entry
  - Strength class choices are the tabulated classes: Given the vocabulary row "class" Then its choices equal the classes of the strength table in order
  - A seeded case of any entry has no input issue: Given a case seeded from each catalogue entry When it is evaluated Then no check reports an input issue
  - Searching the EN 1995 catalogue for "<query>": When the catalogue is searched for "<query>" Then the result contains "<id>"
  - A failing bending case sizes its width: Given a document with the glulam bending case "over" with M_y = 900 kNm on 200 mm by 400 mm When the document is evaluated Then the checks of "over" cite clause 6.1.6 and fail And the governing check offers "at least" on cases[id=over].numbers[id=b].value with required = current x utilisation
  - Invalid inputs fail with a remedy: Given a bending case with the strength class "GL99z" and an input outside the vocabulary When the case is evaluated Then the class check fails with a one-of remedy that lists "GL24h" and the unknown input fails
  - A hole is dragged by position and diameter: Given a document with the hole "cutout-2" at x = 1.0 m, 0.2 m above the bottom, diameter 50 mm When its three grips are read Then they write cutouts[id=cutout-2].distanceM, centreHeightM and lengthM in metres and each grip evaluated at its own anchor returns the stored value
  - A notch depth is dragged through the mirrored effective depth: Given a document with the notch "cutout-1" of depth 60 mm on a 400 mm deep member When the effective-depth grip is dragged to 300 mm Then it writes cutouts[id=cutout-1].depthM = 0.1 m
  - A fastener pattern is edited by dragging rows and columns: Given a pattern of 4 columns and 2 rows with a1 = 80 mm, a2 = 40 mm, a3 = 100 mm, a4 = 40 mm When the grips are read Then column i writes spacingParallelM = (x - a3) / i for i = 1 to 3, row 1 writes spacingPerpendicularM, there is no grip beyond the pattern, and the count steppers write columns and lines
  - Minimum spacing colours every fastener: Given the same pattern When all four spacings are 500 mm Then every fastener demand (required / provided over a1, a2, a3,t and a4,c of the Tables 8.2 to 8.5 of the kernel) is below 1 And when a1 is 5 mm every fastener demand exceeds 1 and the part reads that the minimum spacing is violated
  - A remedy on a unit-converted input is one click: Given a failing notch whose width remedy is computed in millimetres When the remedy is read Then it is applicable, its current value is the stored width in metres and applying it writes the converted required value
  - An entity unit reads only what it references: Given a document with two members and a fastener pattern on the first When the unit of the pattern is read Then it covers the first member row, the connection row and the id columns, and not the second member
  - A CLT panel is a list of typed layers: Given a panel with five layers of 40 mm alternating longitudinal and transverse When the document is evaluated Then T-97 and T-107 read n_layers = 5, t1 to t5 in millimetres and o1 to o5 as 1 for longitudinal and 0 for transverse, and a panel without layers fails the check "en1995.clt.layers" on panels[id=panel-1].layers
  - A layer thickness grip writes its own layer row: Given the panel above When its grips are read Then the grip t3 writes panels[id=panel-1].layers[id=layer-3].thicknessM in metres, returns the stored thickness at its anchor, and no grip writes a case input
  - The laminate follows the rows: Given the panel above When the orientation of layer 2 is longitudinal and the thickness of layer 3 is 60 mm Then the drawn laminate has the grain along the span for layer 2 and a thickness of 60 mm for layer 3
  - Layer grades and symmetry are reported: Given a panel whose layer 3 has the grade C16 beside the panel class C24 Then the warning "en1995.clt.mixed-grade" reports that the panel class is used And a layup of an even number of layers or with different outer layers gets the warning "en1995.clt.symmetry"
  - The layered section agrees with sectionproperties: Given the three-layer panel 30/40/30 mm and the five-layer panel 5 x 40 mm with E = 11000 N/mm2 When the rolling shear modulus is made very large Then the stiffness of the gamma-method equals the composite stiffness of sectionproperties to 1e-6 And when the rolling shear modulus is made vanishing it equals the sum of the own second moments of the longitudinal layers
  - Irregular fastener positions replace the regular pattern: Given a fastener row with the positions (100, 40), (170, 40) and (300, 80.5) mm When the checks run Then the count is 3, the longest row holds 2, a1 = 70 mm between the neighbours of one row, a2 = 40.5 mm between the rows, a3,t = 100 mm and a4,c = 40 mm, and no spacing grip is offered
  - Every explicit position has one grip per coordinate: Given the same row When its grips are read Then px k writes fasteners[id=fastener-1].positions[id=pk].xM and py k writes yM in metres and each returns the stored value at its anchor
  - The spacing colouring uses the actual distances: Given the same row When the second fastener moves to 4 mm from the first in the same row Then both demands exceed 1 And a pair is admissible when it keeps a1 along the grain or a2 across it
  - A diaphragm, a truss and a bracing are typed entities: Given the demo document with the wall diaphragm "diaphragm-1", the Warren truss "truss-1" and the plan bracing "bracing-1" When the document is evaluated Then the checks "en1995.t-94.racking", "en1995.t-95.bracing_capacity" and "en1995.t-96.bracing_force" address diaphragms[id=diaphragm-1], trusses[id=truss-1] and bracings[id=bracing-1], and every check that reads the unverified stabilising divisor lists "ndp.en1995.bracing.stabilising-divisor"
  - A floor diaphragm reads its own inputs: Given the wall diaphragm above When its kind is changed to floor Then the check "en1995.t-94.diaphragm_shear" appears and "en1995.t-94.racking" disappears
  - A bracing needs its member and a truss needs two bays: Given a bracing on a missing member and a truss with one bay Then the checks "en1995.integrity.dangling.bracings.memberId.bracing-1" and "en1995.trusses.layout.truss-1" fail on the entity fields
  - Truss layouts are statically determinate: Given the Warren, Pratt and Howe layouts with 2 to 12 bays and the king-post layout Then twice the number of joints minus three equals the number of members
  - The drawing follows the rows: Given the three entities above When the scene is projected Then each sheathing panel, fastener line, truss member, joint and stabilised member is a part of its entity and each entity offers grips
  - PyNite agrees with the truss and the bracing: Given the 12 m Warren and Pratt trusses of 1.5 m height with six bays under 4 kN/m When PyNite solves the pin-jointed frames Then the largest top chord force equals q l2 / (8 h) = 48 kN and both layouts have the joints and members of the library And for a restraint line of 6 m with N_d = 20 kN and k_br = 500 N/mm the sum of the spring reactions equals q_d l
  - Closed value sets are enums: Given a taper, a cut-out, a CLT layer, a diaphragm, a truss and a bracing Then their kind, tension side, face, orientation, method and product fields accept only the listed values with their English and German labels, an unknown value is refused at the snapshot, in the SQLite database and by the mutation, and a strength grade must be an id of the strength-class catalogue or the check "en1995.catalogue.strength-class" fails with the catalogue as options
